<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-A$ fall could put pressure on inflation-govt.</title>
<headline>RTRS-A$ fall could put pressure on inflation-govt.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Treasurer Peter Costello said on Wednesday the recent fall in the value of the Australian currency could put modest upward pressure on the underlying inflation rate.</p>
<p>&quot;The recent depreciation, if sustained, could be expected to place some modest upward pressure on underlying inflation in the year ahead,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
</text>
